Exactly. And attitude is more than mood. It’s orientation toward reality.

The frog sees a meal. The beetle larva sees an opportunity.

The spider sees its web as a trap for others. The bone-collector caterpillar sees it as a home, a buffet, and a wardrobe.

Same environment. Different interpretations. Different possibilities.

And there’s a beautiful double meaning: in aviation, attitude is your orientation relative to the horizon.

Change your attitude, and you change how you navigate the world.

Not necessarily the reality you’re facing, but what you recognize, how you respond, and what becomes possible.

Sometimes evolution doesn’t give an animal a better weapon. It gives it an entirely different way to play the game.